Wrote `candidates/review1/REVIEW.md`.

Note: `qwen35_fast/engine.py` was edited twice by a concurrent process during the review (adding `compile_blocks`, `gdn_pre`, spec counters, and fixing the FLA kwargs and draft-chain position). I reviewed the current 376-line revision (`md5 13ceca4…`) and flagged which findings were already addressed.

Remaining findings:
1. `_argmax` (line 265) upcasts bf16 logits to fp32 before argmax; HF greedy argmaxes bf16 logits, so near-ties can diverge. Fix: drop `.float()`.
2. CUDA-graph capture (lines 334-344): the two warmup `_step_impl()` calls execute and advance `n`/pending/drafts/KV/GDN state before `replay()`, so the first `generate()` on a fresh engine skips two steps. Fix: snapshot/restore state around warmup or re-prefill after capture. (Also, `stat_steps`/`stat_acc` are incremented inside the captured region.)
3. FLA `fused_recurrent_gated_delta_rule` positional-arg bug (documented; now keyword-fixed).
4. `_draft_chain` MTP position off-by-one (documented; now fixed).
5. `linear_num_key_heads` ignored — latent GVA assumption, safe for this checkpoint.
6. Minor: unused `tok`, `pre_norm` option inconsistent with the reference, `reset()` not clearing KV caches.

I also included a checklist of the areas I verified as matching the reference (norm order/dtype, RoPE layout/dims, q/k norm placement, attention gate, GQA, conv state/activation, gated delta rule args, gated RMSNorm, residual structure, KV indexing, acceptance/rollback) and confirmed there are no host syncs/data-dependent shapes/Python ints from device tensors in `_step_impl`.
